			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Share-Based Compensation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;Subsequent to the Acquisition, the Company has authorized 1,000,000 Class B Profit Interest Units (PIUs) which are equity awards granted to certain employees, providing them with a stake in the appreciation of the Company's equity value. The Company has evaluated its Class B profit interest awards under ASC 718, Compensation - Stock Compensation (ASC 718) and determined that they qualify as share-based payments. These awards provide participants with subordinated distribution rights in the event of a liquidity event, allowing them to benefit from the appreciation in the Company's equity value. The awards are based, at least in part, on the value of the Company's equity and are subject to repurchase at fair value, supporting their classification under ASC 718. The fair value of these awards is determined using a Black-Scholes model, considering factors such as market conditions and the Company's financial performance. The awards vest over a four-year period contingent upon the employee's continuous employment, with 80% vesting based on time (recognized on a straight-line basis over the requisite service period), and 20% based on performance conditions (recognized on a straight-line basis over the vesting period based on the probable performance outcome. The Company reassesses the probability of achieving the performance targets each reporting period and adjusts compensation expense accordingly). In the event of a sale of the Company, any unvested awards will fully vest, provided the employee remains employed through the sale date. Furthermore, the awards are classified as equity, as they meet the criteria outlined in ASC 718-10-25, including participation in the residual returns of the entity's net assets and retention of vested interests upon termination, unless terminated for cause.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

